{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 27,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.27.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Moreover, Job continued his parable, and said,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.27.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " God liveth, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "who",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hath taken away my judgment; and the Almighty ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "who",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hath afflicted my soul;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.27.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All the while my breath ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in me, and the spirit of God ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in my nostrils;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.27.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My lips shall not speak wickedness, nor my tongue utter deceit.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.27.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Far be it from me that I should justify you: till I die I will not remove my integrity from me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.27.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My righteousness I hold fast, and will not let it go: my heart shall not reproach ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "me",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " so long as I live.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.27.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let my enemy be as the wicked, and he that riseth up against me as the unrighteous.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.27.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For what ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the hope of the hypocrite, though he hath gained, when God taketh away his soul?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.27.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Will God hear his cry when trouble cometh upon him?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.27.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Will he delight himself in the Almighty? will he always call upon God?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.27.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will teach you by the hand of God: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with the Almighty will I not conceal.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.27.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, all ye yourselves have seen ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "; why then are ye thus altogether vain?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.27.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the portion of a wicked man with God, and the heritage of oppressors, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " they shall receive of the Almighty.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.27.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If his children are multiplied, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for the sword: and his offspring shall not be satisfied with bread.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.27.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Those that remain of him shall be buried in death: and his widows shall not weep.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.27.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Though he should heap up silver as the dust, and prepare raiment as the clay?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.27.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He may prepare ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", but the just shall put ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " on, and the innocent shall divide the silver.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.27.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He buildeth his house as a moth, and as a booth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the keeper maketh.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.27.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The rich man shall lie down, but he shall not be gathered: he openeth his eyes, and he ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.27.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Terrors take hold on him as waters, a tempest stealeth him away in the night.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.27.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The east wind carrieth him away, and he departeth: and as a storm hurleth him out of his place.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.27.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "God",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shall cast upon him, and not spare: he would fain flee out of his hand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.27.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shall clap their hands at him, and shall hiss him out of his place.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
